  "body": "## Summary\n\nForge action v1: a TypeScript JavaScript action (`runs.using: node24`, verified against actions/typescript-action) that gates and dispatches a heavy workflow per pull request.\n\n- **Mode** from a repo variable passed as input. `enabled-modes` (default all six) fails safe to the nearest more restrictive enabled mode.\n- **`bypass-labels`**: `,` OR, `+` AND. STOP blocks everything; STANDBY lets bypass labels through; bypassers skip the caps and are not counted.\n- **`limit-by-label`**: JSON array from a variable, glob buckets (`pod:*`), caps per mode, first matching entry wins, one search call per bucket at dispatch, rank by PR number. Unreadable count: 2 retries, then HOLD (`on-count-error`); 401/403/404 fails loudly with the missing permission.\n- Drafts never dispatch, fork PRs are skipped, no clone, `GITHUB_TOKEN` only (`actions: write`, `pull-requests: read`).\n- Outputs: `decision`, `reason`, `mode`, `bucket`, `count`, `cap`, plus `rank`, `privileged`, `dispatched`, `failfast`, `runs-on`, `head-sha`, `held-label`. A job summary is written for every decision.\n- `src/policy/` is pure (no I/O) and can later be published as `@crusiblehq/forge-policy`; `src/github.ts` is the narrow Octokit slice; `src/run.ts` orchestrates.\n- Repo CI: test, check-dist, CodeQL, release (moves the `v1` tag; environment `release`), Dependabot (npm, github-actions). Every third-party action is pinned to a full SHA.\n- Docs: README (10-line drop-in plus our pod-0 config), `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md`, SECURITY, CONTRIBUTING, Apache-2.0.\n\n## Test results\n\n- vitest: 98/98 pass. Coverage: 100% statements and lines, 95.3% branches overall; policy module 97% branches (threshold 90% enforced).\n- Integration tests drive `run()` with a mocked Octokit: dispatch inputs, dedupe, caps, retries, 403, held-label, branch-moved.\n- Golden test: `capPlan` with our table equals ci-mode.ts `capOf` for six modes and pod-0 / pod-1.\n- eslint, prettier, tsc clean. `dist/index.js` rebuilt twice: byte-identical (check-dist). Smoke: `node dist/index.js` outside a PR event fails with a clear message.\n\n## Deviations and notes\n\n- The count uses the REST search API (one call per bucket), per the order. The spec (3.2.3) preferred GraphQL for freshness; search can lag by seconds, and this PR is always counted as itself. Switching is local to `listReady`.\n- Release-on-close redispatch of held PRs (spec 3.2.5) is not in v1; a re-run or the next event re-evaluates.\n- Not done by the lane: no release, no tag, no merge.\n\n## Forge master steps\n\n- Review and merge this PR. Then publish `v1.0.0` (the `release` environment waits for approval).\n- Set `vars.CI_LIMIT_BY_LABEL` in the consuming repo from the README.\n- The FORGE app installation does not cover this repo yet (the app token has no push access); this lane used the PAT.\n- Enable branch protection / CodeQL default setup as wanted.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
